{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And she obtained kindness.</b> The kindness abides with her; it does not depart from her." "<b>And he sped.</b> The meaning is haste." "<b>Her portions.</b> Shares, like מנה אחת (one portion) in the language of eating, because she was designated for it." "<b>And seven maidens.</b> They attend her." "<b>Fitting.</b> This expression is known in the words of the Rabbis." "<b>And he changed.</b> He changed the portions to do her good. And the meaning of בית הנשים (house of the women) connects with וישנה, for he changed her portions and her maidens while she was in the house of the women with her companions. Some say that Mordecai did not act properly, for he commanded Esther not to tell, because he feared lest the king take her as wife if he knew that she was of the exile. And afterward they said that by way of prophecy or in a dream he knew that salvation would come through her for Israel. But the correct view in my eyes is that Mordecai did this so that she would keep the Torah of HaShem in secret — that she not eat nevelot and would keep the Sabbaths — and the attendants would not notice; for if the matter became known, perhaps the king would force her or kill her, for she was seized against her will. And we know that Mordecai was among the great ones of Israel, for behold, he was third among the officers who went up with Zerubbabel. And when he saw that the House was not rebuilt, he came to Elam and was at the king's gate in the palace, and this is a high position. And behold, Daniel placed his colleagues over the kingdom of Babylon, and he was at the king's gate. And had Mordecai not been, prior to the affair of Esther, one of the king's servants, the attendants would not have allowed him to walk before the court of the house of the women."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {5 "Reading 'she was designated for it' (שמינה, from שום) for the final clause; the sense is that her special portions were because she was singled out."}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:52.364841204Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}